{"content_hash": "cda327959692403e", "version_id": 589, "article_id": 59, "level_code": "ja_n2", "lang": "ja", "level": 4, "level_label": "N2 中高級", "title": "イラン戦争がヒーリー財務相の予算案を脅かすと研究所が警告", "title_zh": "智库警告：伊朗战争给英国财相的预算计划添乱", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "bbc_business", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm78pwdp3n5qo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1693139062697-f5f8663217fa?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8aXJhbiUyMHdhciUyMHRocmVhdGVuc3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNzY1NjgyfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by sina drakhshani on Unsplash", "author": "sina drakhshani", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@sina_drakhshani?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/flag-of-iran-waving-9S96Rqy9Q1U?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(107, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(145, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "56335abab054"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 248, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "アメリカとイスラエルによるイラン戦争で物価が急上昇し、ヒーリー財務相の初の予算編成に大きな影響が出ている。有力シンクタンクの財政研究所（IFS）が警告を発した。", "lead_zh": "美国和以色列对伊朗的战争导致物价飞涨，给英国财相希利首次编制预算带来巨大压力。有影响力的智库财政研究所（IFS）就此发出警告。", "preview": "IFSによると、予想を上回るインフレにより、政府が公共サービスに充てる予定だった財源が削られる可能性がある。その結果、ヒーリー財務相は支出削減か増税か、あるいはその両方を選ばざるを得なくなるという。同研究所は、予算を帳尻合わせのために非現実的な将来の削減案で埋めるのではなく、信頼", "preview_zh": "IFS指出，高于预期的通胀可能侵蚀政府原本计划用于公共服务的资金。因此，财相希利将不得不在削减支出、增税或两者兼施之间做出选择。该研究所敦促政府提出可信的支出计划，而不是用不现实的未来削减方案来让预算数字凑合过关。财政部拒绝就“谣言和猜测”置评。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 577, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/59/ja_n2.mp3", "duration": 51.65, "size_bytes": 313632, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 158, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@aa22245/content/data/versions/589.json", "paragraphs": ["IFSによると、予想を上回るインフレにより、政府が公共サービスに充てる予定だった財源が削られる可能性がある。その結果、ヒーリー財務相は支出削減か増税か、あるいはその両方を選ばざるを得なくなるという。同研究所は、予算を帳尻合わせのために非現実的な将来の削減案で埋めるのではなく、信頼できる支出計画を示すよう求めた。財務省は「噂や憶測」についてはコメントを拒否した。", "ヒーリー財務相は、今週の国際通貨基金（IMF）総会を前に「中東やヨーロッパでの紛争の影響が世界中の国々に及んでおり、ガソリン価格の上昇や住宅ローン金利の負担増を招いている」と述べた。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["IFS指出，高于预期的通胀可能侵蚀政府原本计划用于公共服务的资金。因此，财相希利将不得不在削减支出、增税或两者兼施之间做出选择。该研究所敦促政府提出可信的支出计划，而不是用不现实的未来削减方案来让预算数字凑合过关。财政部拒绝就“谣言和猜测”置评。", "希利在参加本周的国际货币基金组织（IMF）年会前表示：“中东和欧洲冲突的后果正在冲击世界各国，导致油价上涨、国内房贷更贵。”他强调“英国和盟友能够共同应对这些挑战”，并称他的预算“将通过财政纪律增强经济韧性，给民众喘息空间”。"], "body": "IFSによると、予想を上回るインフレにより、政府が公共サービスに充てる予定だった財源が削られる可能性がある。その結果、ヒーリー財務相は支出削減か増税か、あるいはその両方を選ばざるを得なくなるという。同研究所は、予算を帳尻合わせのために非現実的な将来の削減案で埋めるのではなく、信頼できる支出計画を示すよう求めた。財務省は「噂や憶測」についてはコメントを拒否した。\n\nヒーリー財務相は、今週の国際通貨基金（IMF）総会を前に「中東やヨーロッパでの紛争の影響が世界中の国々に及んでおり、ガソリン価格の上昇や住宅ローン金利の負担増を招いている」と述べた。", "body_zh": "IFS指出，高于预期的通胀可能侵蚀政府原本计划用于公共服务的资金。因此，财相希利将不得不在削减支出、增税或两者兼施之间做出选择。该研究所敦促政府提出可信的支出计划，而不是用不现实的未来削减方案来让预算数字凑合过关。财政部拒绝就“谣言和猜测”置评。\n\n希利在参加本周的国际货币基金组织（IMF）年会前表示：“中东和欧洲冲突的后果正在冲击世界各国，导致油价上涨、国内房贷更贵。”他强调“英国和盟友能够共同应对这些挑战”，并称他的预算“将通过财政纪律增强经济韧性，给民众喘息空间”。", "text": "IFSによると、予想を上回るインフレにより、政府が公共サービスに充てる予定だった財源が削られる可能性がある。その結果、ヒーリー財務相は支出削減か増税か、あるいはその両方を選ばざるを得なくなるという。同研究所は、予算を帳尻合わせのために非現実的な将来の削減案で埋めるのではなく、信頼できる支出計画を示すよう求めた。財務省は「噂や憶測」についてはコメントを拒否した。 ヒーリー財務相は、今週の国際通貨基金（IMF）総会を前に「中東やヨーロッパでの紛争の影響が世界中の国々に及んでおり、ガソリン価格の上昇や住宅ローン金利の負担増を招いている」と述べた。", "vocab": [{"word": "財務相", "pos": "noun", "zh": "财政大臣/财相", "note": "英国政府中负责财政的大臣", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "予算", "pos": "noun", "zh": "预算", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "インフレ", "pos": "noun", "zh": "通货膨胀", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "シンクタンク", "pos": "noun", "zh": "智库", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "警告", "pos": "noun", "zh": "警告", "note": "する动词形：警告する", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "支出", "pos": "noun", "zh": "支出", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "削減", "pos": "noun", "zh": "削减", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "増税", "pos": "noun", "zh": "增税", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "財政規律", "pos": "noun", "zh": "财政纪律", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "借入コスト", "pos": "noun", "zh": "借贷成本", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "債務", "pos": "noun", "zh": "债务", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "転嫁", "pos": "noun", "zh": "转嫁", "note": "する动词形：転嫁する", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "余裕", "pos": "noun", "zh": "余量、缓冲空间", "note": "此处指财政余量", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "一時的", "pos": "adj", "zh": "暂时的", "note": "な形容词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Iran war threatens Healey's Budget plans, think tank warns", "summary_original": "The impact of the Iran war poses significant risks for the government’s spending plans, the Institute for Fiscal Studies says.", "body_original": "Iran war threatens Healey's Budget plans, think tank warns\nBy\nDharshini David\n,\nDeputy economics editor\nand\nTom Espiner\n,\nBusiness reporter\nPublished\n1 hour ago\nThe price spike caused by the US-Israel war in Iran poses a major challenge for Chancellor John Healey as he puts together his first Budget, an influential think tank has warned.\nHigher-than-expected inflation could eat into what the government hoped to spend on public services, meaning Healey will have to choose between spending cuts, tax rises, or a mixture of both, the Institute for Fiscal Studies (IFS) said.\nIt urged the government to ensure its spending plans are credible, as opposed to proposing unrealistic future cuts to make the Budget add up.\nThe Treasury declined to comment on \"rumour and speculation\".\nHowever, speaking ahead of the annual International Monetary Fund meeting this week, Healey said: \"The consequences of conflict in the Middle East and Europe are hitting countries worldwide, leading to higher prices at the pumps and more expensive mortgages at home.\n\"But Britain and our allies can face up to these challenges together.\"\nHe said his Budget \"will build on this approach with fiscal discipline helping to deliver economic resilience\" and give people \"breathing space\".\nHowever, the government is under growing pressure to show financial markets that it has a tight grip on finances as the cost of borrowing rises.\nThe IFS cautioned Healey about making any spending announcements in the 28 October Budget speech he has no intention of honouring.\n\"A 'steady-as-she-goes' Budget is not an option available to the chancellor,\" said IFS director Helen Miller said.\n\"Choosing to stay the course with the inherited tax and spending plans would mean allowing inflation to blow departments' spending plans off course.\n\"Simply pencilling in implicit cuts that he has no intention of delivering would make the Budget a work of fiction,\" she added.\nThe US-Israel war against Iran and Russia's invasion of Ukraine have together helped drive up energy prices around the world.\nThese higher costs have been passed to customers via higher prices on shelves and at the pumps.\nThe wars have also contributed to a rise in the cost of UK government debt interest payments, adding to the pressure on Healey.\nAlthough higher inflation will boost tax revenues, it will also eat into the value of departments' cash budgets, the IFS said.\n'Breathing space'\nLike other analysts, the IFS thinks recent turbulence on bond markets and higher inflation will add around £10bn to forecasts for the government's borrowing costs in 2029-30.\nHowever, it still expects the government to meet its self-imposed fiscal rules - that it will only borrow for investment projects by the financial year 2029-30 and also be reducing debt as a percentage of GDP - not least as inflation pushes up tax revenues.\nBut it expects those rules to be met by a smaller buffer - known as \"headroom\" - of around £20bn. That is less than the £24bn buffer predicted at the time of the Spring Statement by the official forecaster, the Office for Budget Responsibility (OBR).\nRecent indications have been that the markets would be comfortable with that degree of reduced headroom. The IFS also expects any \"breathing space\" help for households to be temporary and limited in scale.\nHowever, the IFS warns that in such a volatile environment, its forecasts are exceptionally uncertain. And the official forecast from the OBR - which the chancellor relies on when making his plans - may come to a very different conclusion.\nThe IFS reckons that to maintain departments' budgets in the face of higher inflation, the government may need to find an extra £25bn in 2029-30.\nThat is before consider considering the ambition to raise defence spending. Raising such an amount would point to significant tax rises.\nThe chancellor does not have to address spending totals in this Budget, and may choose to leave such decisions until future events - for example, next year's Spring Statement or Spending Review - by which time the outlook for the economy could look very different.\nBut the IFS warned that the spending plans inherited from the previous chancellor, Rachel Reeves, would mean some departments' budgets would not keep pace with inflation in a few years time.\nIt said not addressing this would cast doubt on the credibility of the government's plans.\nHowever, previous chancellors have relied on a similar strategy of pencilling in unrealistic future spending plans to ensure that they meet the fiscal rules on the day - only to change the plans further down the line.\nRelated topics\nUK economy\nInstitute for Fiscal Studies\nJohn Healey\nMore on this story\nWhat is the Budget and what could be in it?\nPublished\n3 days ago", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:41:21.254686", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "IFS", "s": 0.163, "e": 0.875, "sm": 162, "em": 875, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "に", "s": 0.887, "e": 1.012, "sm": 887, "em": 1012, "cs": 3, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "よる", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.275, "s